WEBVTT

00:42.083 --> 00:46.963
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

00:47.046 --> 00:48.465
PAIK UI-YONG AND PAIK SA-EON
DNA NOT MATCHED

00:48.548 --> 00:49.799
Did you know already?

00:52.343 --> 00:53.428
It doesn't matter?

00:56.347 --> 00:57.474
If…

00:58.558 --> 01:00.351
something happens to me,

01:02.604 --> 01:04.981
and the Paik Sa-eon you've known

01:05.565 --> 01:07.317
disappears from this world,

01:08.860 --> 01:10.070
just remember this.

01:11.404 --> 01:12.447
JUAN FISHING

01:17.827 --> 01:21.498
The only Paik Sa-eon I want to leave
behind in this world is the one

01:23.291 --> 01:24.876
that belongs to Hong Hee-joo.

01:26.086 --> 01:28.254
I know I have no right to say this,

01:28.338 --> 01:29.339
but Hee-joo,

01:30.256 --> 01:31.883
I hope you won't be fooled anymore.

01:32.717 --> 01:36.888
I know your mom forced you to marry him
in my place, and you had no choice,

01:36.971 --> 01:39.516
but if the Paik family deceived us
from the start,

01:39.599 --> 01:41.142
you don't have to stay married to him.

01:44.979 --> 01:47.565
I'll find out the secret
that family is hiding from us.

01:47.649 --> 01:49.484
I'll meet Paik Sa-eon if I have to.

01:52.946 --> 01:54.197
It's my choice.

02:03.164 --> 02:06.334
I wasn't just your stand-in.

02:06.417 --> 02:08.837
It's not because my mom forced me.

02:08.920 --> 02:11.840
I, Hong Hee-joo, choose Paik Sa-eon.

02:12.757 --> 02:13.591
Hee-joo.

02:13.675 --> 02:16.261
And he's not the only one who has secrets.

02:16.845 --> 02:18.763
I've deceived him too.

02:19.848 --> 02:21.933
Including about being able to speak.

02:28.606 --> 02:30.358
So this is what your voice sounds like.

02:33.945 --> 02:35.071
It's pretty.

02:36.531 --> 02:38.324
I don't know how it'd sound to you,

02:39.033 --> 02:40.493
but when we were young,

02:42.328 --> 02:44.581
I liked how you called my name.

02:45.540 --> 02:47.041
Though I hated your mom

02:47.625 --> 02:50.044
and it felt weird to suddenly have
a younger sibling…

02:52.630 --> 02:53.631
"In-a."

02:55.174 --> 02:57.343
Your voice was so adorable.

02:59.220 --> 03:01.931
To have a little sister
who called my name like that…

03:05.268 --> 03:06.853
It was really nice, to be honest.

03:24.162 --> 03:25.163
Who sent you…

03:26.915 --> 03:28.124
this document?

03:30.251 --> 03:31.252
I don't know.

03:31.336 --> 03:33.087
It was sent anonymously.

03:33.171 --> 03:35.548
And it wasn't my dad or your mom.

03:36.215 --> 03:38.009
But I'm certain of one thing.

03:38.760 --> 03:40.053
They knew

03:40.720 --> 03:43.765
I wouldn't marry Paik Sa-eon
if I saw this.

03:44.349 --> 03:47.644
So, someone hoped
the marriage wouldn't go through.

03:50.188 --> 03:51.564
JUAN FISHING

04:19.801 --> 04:21.177
What are you doing here?

04:21.261 --> 04:22.804
We have to get out of here!

04:22.887 --> 04:24.639
He's after you!

04:25.265 --> 04:26.099
Go! Hurry!

04:26.182 --> 04:27.392
No!

04:28.476 --> 04:29.727
Let's go!

04:44.242 --> 04:45.410
PAIK SA-EON

04:53.668 --> 04:55.253
I'd like to report a missing person.

04:55.336 --> 04:56.296
A missing person?

04:56.379 --> 04:59.882
Yes, I can't reach my husband,
and he hasn't come home yet.

05:00.383 --> 05:02.677
How long has it been
since you last heard from him?

05:03.386 --> 05:04.679
About six hours.

05:04.762 --> 05:07.724
Could it be that your husband
is just running a little late?

05:07.807 --> 05:10.685
We can't file a missing person report
based on that alone.

05:10.768 --> 05:11.936
What can I do then?

05:12.020 --> 05:14.772
In fact, an adult over 18
with no history of illness

05:14.856 --> 05:18.276
or evidence of a crime is considered
a runaway, not a missing person…

05:18.359 --> 05:21.779
There is evidence of a crime.
My husband is being threatened.

05:21.863 --> 05:23.031
He's being threatened?

05:23.114 --> 05:26.993
Yes, by a complete madman.
He might've done something to him.

05:27.076 --> 05:29.203
He set a fire and threw a bomb!

05:29.287 --> 05:31.289
He even pushed someone off a cliff.

05:31.372 --> 05:34.375
Threats, bombs,
and he even pushed someone off a cliff?

05:34.459 --> 05:36.419
What's your husband's name?

05:39.255 --> 05:40.214
Hello?

05:40.298 --> 05:43.217
Ma'am, could I have your name
and your husband's name?

05:52.894 --> 05:55.396
PAIK UI-YONG AND PAIK SA-EON
DNA NOT MATCHED

05:57.231 --> 05:59.776
I wonder what his real name is.

06:00.735 --> 06:02.570
What do you think his real name was,

06:02.653 --> 06:04.906
and how did he end up living
as Paik Sa-eon?

06:04.989 --> 06:07.700
When I first met Paik Sa-eon,

06:07.784 --> 06:09.535
he was 15 years old.

06:10.369 --> 06:12.121
I had never seen him before that.

06:13.081 --> 06:13.915
Yes.

06:15.208 --> 06:16.959
That was strange to me.

06:17.543 --> 06:20.296
Paik Ui-yong had a son
who was two years older than I was.

06:21.089 --> 06:23.299
He was living next door,
but I'd never seen him.

06:26.177 --> 06:27.720
I think I understand now.

06:28.513 --> 06:32.183
I see why his parents
treated him like a stranger.

06:33.434 --> 06:35.019
There was no affection at all.

06:35.853 --> 06:37.230
Maybe there's a biological son?

06:38.106 --> 06:39.774
If the current Paik Sa-eon

06:40.399 --> 06:42.944
became their son at the age of 15,

06:43.528 --> 06:45.613
then who was Paik Sa-eon before that?

06:45.696 --> 06:47.657
And why did they hide him?

06:50.201 --> 06:51.994
EPISODE 9

06:56.916 --> 06:59.585
- Why are you here at this hour?
- Did you come alone?

06:59.669 --> 07:01.003
Where's Sa-eon?

07:04.215 --> 07:05.466
Report it for me.

07:08.010 --> 07:10.930
Sa-eon hasn't come home,
and I can't reach him.

07:12.932 --> 07:14.225
How are you talking?

07:14.851 --> 07:15.685
Mr. Min.

07:21.357 --> 07:22.942
Chairman Paik

07:23.734 --> 07:26.320
was known for doting on his grandson.

07:26.946 --> 07:32.076
So, why did he keep his beloved grandson
hidden until he was 15?

07:34.537 --> 07:35.580
There was a reason

07:35.663 --> 07:38.040
his biological grandson
couldn't be shown to the world.

07:39.167 --> 07:41.419
Is that why he presented
a flawless fake grandson?

07:41.502 --> 07:42.545
Fake?

07:42.628 --> 07:43.463
I…

07:44.297 --> 07:46.716
have lived as Paik Sa-eon's wife
for three years,

07:47.800 --> 07:49.385
and I only found out now.

07:50.553 --> 07:52.513
That he's not your biological son.

07:52.597 --> 07:54.307
Where do you get off saying that?

07:54.390 --> 07:56.058
You must be mistaken.

07:56.642 --> 07:58.644
You're not Sa-eon's real wife

07:59.270 --> 08:00.188
but the stand-in.

08:01.189 --> 08:02.899
Yeah, you're right.

08:02.982 --> 08:05.026
Sa-eon's just a stand-in too.

08:05.109 --> 08:05.943
Honey.

08:06.027 --> 08:07.945
That's true, but he's different.

08:09.572 --> 08:11.240
Isn't he

08:11.324 --> 08:14.076
important and necessary to you both?

08:15.203 --> 08:18.748
So find out right now
what happened to him.

08:23.211 --> 08:24.545
Yes, I understand.

08:34.430 --> 08:38.100
There have been no reports filed
under the spokesperson's name as of now.

08:43.147 --> 08:44.065
Did you hear that?

08:44.649 --> 08:45.566
Go home.

08:51.447 --> 08:52.281
Fine.

08:53.366 --> 08:56.786
I admit that Sa-eon
is very important and necessary to us.

08:57.370 --> 08:59.580
So we won't just sit idly by, will we?

09:10.716 --> 09:12.843
When did she start talking?

09:14.095 --> 09:15.179
Did you know?

09:24.480 --> 09:25.314
Excuse me.

09:28.901 --> 09:30.736
How much does the spokesperson know

09:32.113 --> 09:33.906
about the person making the threats?

09:35.032 --> 09:36.534
What do you mean, "how much"?

09:38.786 --> 09:40.621
Everything he told the police.

09:44.542 --> 09:46.961
So nothing more about the heterochromia?

09:48.754 --> 09:49.589
What…

09:51.132 --> 09:52.425
should he know?

10:07.315 --> 10:09.317
When Mr. Paik was young,

10:10.067 --> 10:11.819
he had eye surgery.

10:12.987 --> 10:14.572
It's a little-known fact.

10:15.698 --> 10:16.949
Since then,

10:19.035 --> 10:20.953
his eyes were no longer different colors.

10:31.964 --> 10:34.925
What about you, Sis? Do you know him well?

10:35.009 --> 10:36.010
Listen carefully.

10:37.595 --> 10:38.971
In this world,

10:39.639 --> 10:42.600
the person who knows Paik Sa-eon
the best is me.

10:46.270 --> 10:48.648
When Paik Sa-eon first came to this house,

10:49.231 --> 10:51.400
he was like a scared stray cat.

10:51.484 --> 10:54.862
I've never seen him
smile comfortably in this house.

10:55.821 --> 10:56.822
I've always

10:57.657 --> 10:58.824
felt sorry for him.

11:04.455 --> 11:05.373
SANG-WOO

11:17.176 --> 11:18.094
Hello?

11:18.177 --> 11:19.178
J&P SEOUL HOSPITAL

11:35.236 --> 11:37.279
Where is he? Is he in surgery?

11:37.863 --> 11:39.031
Yes, it's been two hours.

11:40.032 --> 11:42.201
Was he hurt badly? Where and how bad…

11:42.284 --> 11:43.452
Hee-joo, calm down.

11:44.078 --> 11:45.538
- Take a seat.
- No, I…

11:52.211 --> 11:55.631
What is this? What in the world happened?

11:57.091 --> 11:59.051
JUAN FISHING

12:14.608 --> 12:15.734
Mr. Jeong Jin-seok?

12:17.611 --> 12:19.697
I came to ask you something.

12:21.073 --> 12:22.324
Are you a cop?

12:28.747 --> 12:29.915
My name's Ji Sang-woo.

12:30.958 --> 12:32.626
I'm doing a show and covering

12:32.710 --> 12:35.421
the missing children case
from Sinil Childcare Center.

12:50.519 --> 12:52.229
NEWSCASTER NA YOU-RI

12:53.522 --> 12:54.982
Hello?

12:55.065 --> 12:56.609
I heard from one of the writers

12:56.692 --> 12:59.653
that you found where Jeong Jin-seok lives.

13:00.279 --> 13:01.155
Did you meet him?

13:01.238 --> 13:04.158
I did, but it was pointless.

13:04.241 --> 13:06.118
As soon as I mentioned the villa,

13:06.202 --> 13:07.036
he got scared.

13:07.119 --> 13:08.787
As if he feared the consequences.

13:15.461 --> 13:16.462
And?

13:17.713 --> 13:19.882
Hello?

13:20.424 --> 13:21.425
Sang-woo?

13:32.645 --> 13:34.730
JUAN FISHING

13:44.490 --> 13:45.699
Mr. Paik Sa-eon?

13:46.700 --> 13:48.035
Mr. Jeong Jin-seok?

13:48.118 --> 13:49.411
Mr. Jeong!

14:18.274 --> 14:20.025
This is about how the fire started,

14:20.109 --> 14:23.946
who set it, and why Paik Sa-eon was there.

14:24.822 --> 14:27.241
Also, your relationship with Paik Sa-eon.

14:28.951 --> 14:30.619
I don't know any of that.

14:31.996 --> 14:32.997
But…

14:34.957 --> 14:38.043
I couldn't ignore the non-stop ringing
of his phone.

14:44.717 --> 14:45.551
Thank you.

14:47.761 --> 14:48.596
And…

14:52.266 --> 14:53.350
I'm sorry, Sang-woo.

14:55.102 --> 14:56.520
I've kept so many things from you.

15:00.524 --> 15:02.735
- Is it over?
- Yeah.

15:02.818 --> 15:05.571
For now, let's wait and see
until he wakes up.

15:07.448 --> 15:08.282
All right, then.

15:50.532 --> 15:52.159
It must've hurt.

15:55.996 --> 15:57.414
It must've been scary.

16:03.963 --> 16:05.381
You must've been lonely.

16:06.215 --> 16:09.885
When I was hurt, scared, and lonely,

16:11.553 --> 16:13.555
you watched over me…

16:16.100 --> 16:17.518
and ran to me.

16:18.435 --> 16:19.520
But that girl

16:21.355 --> 16:22.356
had no one

16:23.816 --> 16:25.442
to rely on, anywhere.

16:26.694 --> 16:28.696
I wanted to help her escape.

16:29.279 --> 16:30.614
Hoping that she could

16:31.949 --> 16:33.617
leave that house and live freely.

16:33.701 --> 16:37.663
And if you can, tell Hee-joo for me.

16:37.746 --> 16:39.039
Tell her not to worry.

16:39.623 --> 16:42.376
Tell her I'll be right there!

16:42.459 --> 16:43.293
Tell me

16:43.877 --> 16:45.713
how to hate you.

16:46.880 --> 16:49.049
Tell me how to not love you.

16:51.468 --> 16:52.886
It's my turn now.

16:52.970 --> 16:55.639
It's my turn to protect you.

16:58.559 --> 17:00.894
So, please wake up. Please.

17:11.822 --> 17:13.699
DR. JI SANG-WOO

17:14.908 --> 17:16.827
Thanks for waiting!

17:17.953 --> 17:19.038
Eat up.

17:19.997 --> 17:21.707
So, Crime Report. Right?

17:22.499 --> 17:25.753
Did you receive any tip-off
about the Sinil Childcare Center?

17:27.963 --> 17:29.965
Why are you interested in that?

17:30.049 --> 17:31.050
What?

17:31.133 --> 17:33.218
I'm already upset enough as it is.

17:34.136 --> 17:36.472
Why treat me on a day
when I have no appetite, of all days?

17:36.555 --> 17:37.389
Eat.

17:37.473 --> 17:39.641
- Why?
- Try this too.

17:40.726 --> 17:42.978
What is it? Just tell me.

17:43.062 --> 17:44.271
Well…

17:48.150 --> 17:49.693
Do you want to look into it yourself?

17:50.652 --> 17:51.487
Me?

17:54.114 --> 17:56.700
Sure, take your time. Eat up.

18:01.455 --> 18:04.083
Who, what, when, where,

18:04.166 --> 18:07.002
how, and why it happened.

18:12.883 --> 18:13.884
I'll give you the source.

18:13.967 --> 18:15.636
Source?

18:16.470 --> 18:18.055
- What is it?
- Well…

18:29.817 --> 18:31.318
- Twins?
- Come on.

19:10.941 --> 19:12.192
UNEXPLAINED FIRE IN JEONGI-DONG

19:12.276 --> 19:13.110
DID YOU DO THIS?

19:16.113 --> 19:17.573
I WARNED YOU NOT TO ACT ALONE

19:17.656 --> 19:19.199
I CAN'T CLEAN UP ALL YOUR MESS

19:19.283 --> 19:21.076
YOU'RE LUCKY PAIK SA-EON IS ALIVE

19:21.160 --> 19:22.494
Paik Sa-eon?

19:35.841 --> 19:37.843
I had no idea.

19:39.386 --> 19:40.721
How did you know?

19:42.097 --> 19:44.933
THIS IS YOUR LAST WARNING.
DON'T CAUSE TROUBLE, JUST WAIT.

19:47.019 --> 19:48.353
Last warning?

19:49.813 --> 19:52.232
I think you're the one
who'll cause trouble.

20:45.160 --> 20:46.328
Father.

20:46.411 --> 20:47.746
That old man came again?

20:48.247 --> 20:50.707
- Who was the kid with him?
- I told you not to call me that!

21:00.926 --> 21:02.427
Go to bed early here tonight.

21:03.345 --> 21:04.972
And do not come outside.

21:05.639 --> 21:06.473
Got it?

21:22.906 --> 21:23.740
Help…

21:42.467 --> 21:43.844
I told you not to come out.

21:44.511 --> 21:45.345
Go inside.

21:52.978 --> 21:53.979
Help!

22:30.974 --> 22:33.310
Some monsters are made,

22:34.061 --> 22:35.562
but some are simply born.

22:36.605 --> 22:38.106
It was bad luck.

22:38.815 --> 22:41.485
How dare something like that
be born into my family?

22:42.360 --> 22:45.155
At first, it was a goldfish,
and then a cat.

22:46.531 --> 22:49.451
Next, it was children younger than him.

22:51.078 --> 22:52.329
What kept increasing

22:53.121 --> 22:56.500
were the black bags filled with the dead.

22:57.626 --> 22:59.503
But it's okay now.

23:00.420 --> 23:03.298
That bastard ended up
in one of those bags too.

23:05.842 --> 23:09.137
And now,
I'll fill the place of my grandson…

23:13.391 --> 23:16.353
with whomever I please.

23:18.772 --> 23:19.689
Child,

23:20.440 --> 23:23.860
do you know why I didn't give you a name?

23:33.537 --> 23:34.412
It's okay.

23:35.831 --> 23:36.748
It's okay.

23:36.832 --> 23:37.666
It's okay.

23:38.667 --> 23:39.501
It's okay.

23:40.377 --> 23:41.419
It's okay.

23:48.218 --> 23:49.469
Are you okay?

23:49.553 --> 23:51.096
Are you feeling better?

23:51.721 --> 23:52.556
Hee-joo.

23:54.808 --> 23:56.476
Yeah, it's me.

23:57.269 --> 23:58.103
Can you see me?

24:02.566 --> 24:04.067
I'll get the doctor.

24:06.403 --> 24:08.947
I could hear your voice.

24:10.073 --> 24:10.907
"It's okay."

24:13.869 --> 24:15.704
You told me that.

24:17.122 --> 24:17.956
Yeah.

24:19.958 --> 24:21.877
It's really okay now.

24:25.964 --> 24:27.424
I'll go get the doctor.

24:30.677 --> 24:31.678
Hee-joo.

24:31.761 --> 24:33.180
He just woke up.

24:33.263 --> 24:34.431
Is that so?

24:47.736 --> 24:48.737
How are you feeling?

24:51.698 --> 24:52.782
I'm fine.

24:52.866 --> 24:54.201
I doubt that.

24:55.535 --> 24:56.995
This is my father's hospital.

24:57.579 --> 25:00.290
I made sure word wouldn't get out,
so you can relax

25:00.373 --> 25:01.917
and receive proper treatment.

25:04.169 --> 25:05.462
What about

25:06.171 --> 25:07.714
the person who was with me?

25:10.383 --> 25:11.760
Is he alive?

26:00.642 --> 26:02.310
Let me ask this first.

26:03.228 --> 26:05.230
What's your relationship
with Jeong Jin-seok?

26:05.981 --> 26:07.565
He raised me.

26:08.817 --> 26:11.027
His original name's Jeong Sang-hun.

26:11.611 --> 26:12.862
I'd been looking for so long

26:14.072 --> 26:15.657
without knowing that he had changed it.

26:17.867 --> 26:19.286
He raised you?

26:22.539 --> 26:23.581
It's a long story.

26:24.708 --> 26:26.084
Complicated and personal.

26:26.167 --> 26:28.211
Is Hee-joo involved
in this personal matter?

26:30.755 --> 26:31.756
Hee-joo

26:32.966 --> 26:35.218
is my only family and guardian.

26:36.261 --> 26:39.139
It's not an inappropriate relationship.

26:40.265 --> 26:41.099
So don't worry.

26:41.933 --> 26:44.269
If it's not, then why do you hide it?

26:49.899 --> 26:52.068
Why should I expose Hee-joo to the world?

26:53.695 --> 26:55.363
My complicated personal matters

26:56.114 --> 26:57.657
will be revealed soon.

26:58.616 --> 27:00.577
When people start criticizing me,

27:01.494 --> 27:03.121
do you want them to gossip

27:04.205 --> 27:05.123
about Hee-joo too?

27:24.225 --> 27:25.310
Thank you.

27:27.187 --> 27:29.314
I think I've gotten you wrong.

27:30.065 --> 27:31.316
I apologize.

27:40.241 --> 27:41.743
Can I ask you a favor?

27:42.994 --> 27:43.870
What is it?

27:43.953 --> 27:45.622
Please do everything you can

27:47.499 --> 27:49.334
to help him wake up.

27:50.085 --> 27:51.544
He's a key witness

27:52.754 --> 27:54.381
to the Sinil Childcare Center case.

27:54.964 --> 27:56.674
And he provided a crucial tip-off.

27:58.510 --> 27:59.427
A tip-off?

28:01.763 --> 28:03.348
"He's alive."

28:04.015 --> 28:05.350
The real culprit in that case,

28:05.934 --> 28:09.020
the one who's blackmailing me
and sending me death threats.

28:11.439 --> 28:12.607
It's the same person?

28:14.442 --> 28:16.027
I thought he was dead,

28:16.986 --> 28:18.947
but he's alive.

28:31.626 --> 28:32.877
CANDIDATE PAIK UI-YONG'S INTRO

28:37.590 --> 28:38.842
The cameras are ready.

28:40.343 --> 28:41.261
But…

28:41.970 --> 28:45.724
They're asking again
if the spokesperson still can't make it.

28:45.807 --> 28:47.475
Filming starts soon.

28:49.561 --> 28:50.478
What do you think?

28:51.146 --> 28:51.980
I apologize.

28:56.109 --> 28:57.193
Any word from Sa-eon?

28:58.027 --> 28:58.862
No, sir.

28:59.904 --> 29:02.282
Still, there haven't been
any incident reports.

29:02.365 --> 29:03.616
That's good enough.

29:11.374 --> 29:13.084
Did you check what I asked you to?

29:17.964 --> 29:20.550
I have been keeping an eye
on the professor…

29:22.093 --> 29:23.595
Nothing unusual so far.

29:26.598 --> 29:27.891
TEXT MESSAGE

29:44.115 --> 29:45.533
HEE-JOO

29:45.617 --> 29:47.243
Are you still at work?

29:48.411 --> 29:50.205
Will you be late?
You said you'd come early.

29:50.288 --> 29:53.500
I can't reach you. Are you busy?
Why can't I reach you?

29:54.709 --> 29:56.961
It's past 11 p.m. Why aren't you home yet?

29:57.879 --> 29:59.380
And you're not picking up.

30:00.173 --> 30:01.424
Where are you?

30:10.058 --> 30:11.726
PAIK SA-EON

30:14.229 --> 30:16.523
YOU HAVE A NEW VOICEMAIL

30:19.192 --> 30:22.654
You have new messages. First message.

30:22.737 --> 30:24.656
Where are you? Is something wrong?

30:26.950 --> 30:28.785
This has never happened before.

30:30.078 --> 30:32.330
You always let me know
if you're not coming home.

30:32.413 --> 30:35.291
No matter how late,
you always slept at home.

30:36.209 --> 30:38.795
See you at home.

30:40.046 --> 30:42.715
I won't be late.

30:49.764 --> 30:51.933
You said you wouldn't be late.

30:52.016 --> 30:53.685
So, why aren't you home?

31:07.991 --> 31:09.659
I'll check your blood pressure.

31:16.374 --> 31:19.419
Is my guardian outside?

31:20.003 --> 31:21.504
No, no one's outside.

31:32.432 --> 31:33.975
PAIK SA-EON

31:59.334 --> 32:01.127
HEE-JOO

32:02.879 --> 32:04.464
Where did you go?

32:26.235 --> 32:30.031
These crabs were caught
early this morning in Seosan.

32:30.865 --> 32:35.453
My wife's favorite dish is blue crab stew,
so I make it often.

32:35.536 --> 32:37.038
Now,

32:37.622 --> 32:41.000
shall we see how fresh these crabs are?

32:41.709 --> 32:42.543
Okay.

32:44.796 --> 32:45.630
Look at this.

32:46.381 --> 32:47.465
It's still alive.

32:50.426 --> 32:51.719
Look!

33:10.196 --> 33:11.072
See?

33:11.155 --> 33:14.492
Prepping these live crabs
isn't easy, you see.

33:15.368 --> 33:16.202
Honey!

33:17.245 --> 33:21.541
This is what I've done for you
all this time.

33:22.458 --> 33:25.503
Now, you make blue crab stew often
for your wife,

33:26.129 --> 33:29.799
so what do you usually make for your son?

33:29.882 --> 33:31.467
Well… For my son?

33:32.051 --> 33:35.221
Yes, what does the spokesperson like?

33:35.304 --> 33:38.182
He takes after me, so he likes seafood.

33:38.933 --> 33:41.936
When it comes to seafood, he's not picky.

33:47.275 --> 33:50.194
Now, my son couldn't make it today,

33:50.278 --> 33:54.657
so to make up for it,
I invited a special guest.

33:55.450 --> 33:56.951
You can look forward to it.

34:10.048 --> 34:11.049
Welcome.

34:11.132 --> 34:12.508
My daughter-in-law.

34:25.396 --> 34:27.315
BEOMJIN DONGAN POLICE STATION

34:39.827 --> 34:41.079
What are you doing here?

34:45.166 --> 34:46.793
Why did you come in your state?

34:46.876 --> 34:48.044
Why did you come here?

34:55.802 --> 34:57.303
Give me that.

35:09.315 --> 35:11.609
So, why did you lie to me?

35:13.152 --> 35:14.487
I know everything now.

35:15.071 --> 35:16.823
I know you're not Paik Sa-eon.

35:18.407 --> 35:20.785
I even know who the real Paik Sa-eon is.

35:21.786 --> 35:22.954
You're worse than me.

35:23.037 --> 35:26.541
You've deceived me
more doggedly than I did,

35:27.375 --> 35:28.960
and for much longer.

35:29.710 --> 35:31.504
So without knowing anything,

35:33.047 --> 35:36.592
I teamed up with the guy
who tried to ruin you.

35:36.676 --> 35:38.761
I threatened and tormented you.

35:40.680 --> 35:43.182
Who knows what he'll do now?

35:44.559 --> 35:46.144
So I can't just let him be.

35:47.270 --> 35:49.313
- Hee-joo…
- For once!

35:54.235 --> 35:55.236
For once,

35:56.362 --> 35:58.072
I want to protect you.

36:00.575 --> 36:02.160
So that you never suffer…

36:06.622 --> 36:07.874
or get hurt again.

36:10.001 --> 36:10.918
You know what?

36:13.254 --> 36:16.549
You could get hurt and be in danger again
if you stay with me.

36:17.300 --> 36:20.636
But I'm asking you to stay by my side
because I can't let you go.

36:23.472 --> 36:25.099
You still don't get it?

36:25.766 --> 36:29.270
I lived because of you.
I endured because of you.

36:43.159 --> 36:44.160
Hong Hee-joo.

36:45.286 --> 36:46.287
Even if I'm not

36:46.954 --> 36:48.664
the Paik Sa-eon you knew,

36:50.499 --> 36:51.459
does it not matter?

36:57.048 --> 36:58.674
It didn't matter to you either.

36:58.758 --> 37:02.762
Whether I was the Hong Hee-joo
who couldn't speak or could speak,

37:02.845 --> 37:03.846
and even when I was 406,

37:03.930 --> 37:05.181
you knew, but it didn't matter.

37:08.100 --> 37:10.728
I'm happy to finally know the real you.

37:12.271 --> 37:13.105
No.

37:14.065 --> 37:15.942
I'm sorry for realizing it so late.

37:34.627 --> 37:35.753
Did you know?

37:35.836 --> 37:36.879
I did not.

37:37.463 --> 37:40.633
But it seems he and In-a
had been in contact beforehand.

37:44.053 --> 37:45.638
But she is

37:46.764 --> 37:49.225
able to talk and listen now.

38:00.278 --> 38:02.613
I've been curious about this.

38:03.447 --> 38:05.741
Who does Spokesperson Paik take after?

38:07.702 --> 38:10.371
No matter how closely I look at him,

38:10.454 --> 38:12.164
he doesn't resemble either of you.

38:12.873 --> 38:15.501
Come on. What are you talking about?

38:16.168 --> 38:17.253
Back in my prime,

38:17.336 --> 38:21.382
I had big, bright eyes
and a sharp jawline, just like Sa-eon.

38:21.465 --> 38:23.092
- Really?
- Of course.

38:23.175 --> 38:24.677
Then show me some old photos.

38:25.261 --> 38:26.470
Do you have an album?

38:26.554 --> 38:28.180
Don't you want to see

38:28.264 --> 38:30.516
what the spokesperson looked like
as a child?

38:30.599 --> 38:32.184
I bet he was so cute.

38:32.268 --> 38:33.477
- Show us!
- Yeah, show us!

38:33.561 --> 38:35.354
- Show us.
- Yeah, he was cute.

38:35.438 --> 38:36.731
- Excuse me.
- He was cute.

38:36.814 --> 38:38.149
I have a question too.

38:39.025 --> 38:39.900
Since the wedding,

38:40.693 --> 38:41.861
you and the spokesperson

38:41.944 --> 38:44.030
haven't attended
any official events together.

38:44.905 --> 38:46.032
Can I ask you why?

38:49.076 --> 38:52.371
The Paik Sa-eon I knew before the wedding

38:52.455 --> 38:54.790
and the Paik Sa-eon I got to know after…

38:58.210 --> 39:00.212
are two completely different people.

39:01.464 --> 39:02.298
What?

39:03.549 --> 39:05.968
What do you mean by that?

39:08.429 --> 39:12.183
The Paik Sa-eon I knew before the wedding
is this person.

39:13.392 --> 39:15.853
But I later found out

39:16.562 --> 39:18.064
that their son…

39:28.199 --> 39:29.825
Hey, In-a!

39:31.410 --> 39:35.247
This is why daytime drinking is dangerous.
You can't even hold your liquor!

39:38.125 --> 39:39.251
Sir.

39:39.960 --> 39:41.003
A package came for you.

39:41.087 --> 39:42.922
Thank you! Now!

39:43.005 --> 39:45.007
The abalone from Wando is here!

39:45.091 --> 39:48.302
They're fresh and very big!

39:48.386 --> 39:49.261
Open it.

39:49.345 --> 39:50.262
Yes, sir.

39:53.849 --> 39:54.975
- What is that?
- What?

39:55.059 --> 39:57.478
- What is that? That's gross!
- What is that?

41:09.383 --> 41:10.593
Who is it?

41:11.177 --> 41:12.845
It says Dr. Ji Sang-woo.

41:22.730 --> 41:24.064
Sang-woo!

41:27.818 --> 41:28.652
Be careful.

41:31.071 --> 41:32.323
Are you okay?

41:33.616 --> 41:35.576
What? What's that?

41:36.285 --> 41:37.161
What happened?

41:37.828 --> 41:39.163
I got a little hurt.

41:39.246 --> 41:40.080
"A little"?

41:40.873 --> 41:41.957
This isn't a little.

41:42.625 --> 41:43.459
What?

41:44.919 --> 41:46.045
What about there?

41:48.130 --> 41:49.256
What about here?

41:50.007 --> 41:51.091
Well…

41:55.596 --> 41:58.057
- Close your eyes for a second.
- My eyes?

42:02.353 --> 42:03.229
There. Open them.

42:06.023 --> 42:07.358
One eye had camel-like eyelashes.

42:07.441 --> 42:08.984
- Camel?
- Or giraffe?

42:09.068 --> 42:11.487
Is that the only thing you can think of?

42:13.072 --> 42:16.033
I mean, there are other things,
like a peacock.

42:16.116 --> 42:17.159
Sure.

42:17.660 --> 42:18.953
Let's go with peacock.

42:24.124 --> 42:25.501
Wait.

42:25.584 --> 42:27.419
That's not important right now.

42:27.503 --> 42:29.797
This, this, and this.

42:29.880 --> 42:30.714
Well?

42:31.340 --> 42:32.174
Who did this?

42:32.258 --> 42:34.134
It's kind of a long story.

42:34.218 --> 42:35.135
Really?

42:36.804 --> 42:39.306
Then follow me.

42:39.390 --> 42:40.224
Let's go.

42:42.184 --> 42:45.896
It was just a small accident.
There was a fire.

42:46.647 --> 42:47.481
A fire?

42:50.776 --> 42:51.652
That's okay.

42:52.528 --> 42:53.988
- Sorry.
- It didn't splatter much.

42:55.406 --> 42:56.490
Still…

42:57.366 --> 42:58.951
I'd say I was pretty fortunate.

43:03.163 --> 43:06.083
Who started the fire and why?

43:06.959 --> 43:08.127
I'm sorry, but…

43:10.212 --> 43:11.380
I can't tell you yet.

43:11.463 --> 43:14.466
It involves someone's personal life,
and it's not my place to share.

43:19.555 --> 43:21.056
I don't like secrets either.

43:21.140 --> 43:22.057
Sang-woo.

43:25.769 --> 43:26.979
Must you keep…

43:29.440 --> 43:30.649
digging into this case?

43:32.943 --> 43:36.238
The higher-ups are pressuring us
not to air it.

43:37.364 --> 43:39.116
Someone's trying to cover it up.

43:48.709 --> 43:51.962
I never gave consent,
so don't even think about showing my face.

43:54.882 --> 43:55.716
In-a.

44:02.264 --> 44:03.432
What are you doing?

44:03.515 --> 44:05.267
What do you mean?

44:05.851 --> 44:07.978
I came to ask questions
that need to be asked.

44:24.995 --> 44:26.413
Do you need anything?

44:27.581 --> 44:31.085
Stay by my side until I fall asleep.

44:39.843 --> 44:41.345
I'll be right here.

44:45.599 --> 44:47.017
I'm having trouble sleeping.

44:47.935 --> 44:49.019
When I close my eyes,

44:49.687 --> 44:51.980
I have nightmares about fire.

45:07.663 --> 45:11.333
How did you find me earlier?

45:12.751 --> 45:13.752
Give me my phone.

45:24.430 --> 45:25.764
LOCATION SHARING

45:25.848 --> 45:26.849
When did you…

45:30.018 --> 45:31.937
Right after the cliff accident.

45:33.522 --> 45:34.565
I felt anxious.

45:38.902 --> 45:40.487
I want it on my phone too.

45:41.280 --> 45:42.281
I'm anxious too.

45:43.198 --> 45:44.032
Hong Hee-joo.

45:45.409 --> 45:46.743
If…

45:49.496 --> 45:50.998
you can't reach me again

45:51.874 --> 45:53.625
in the future…

45:55.586 --> 45:57.629
or don't know where I am,

45:59.006 --> 46:00.174
don't look for me.

46:00.924 --> 46:01.925
Promise me.

46:03.760 --> 46:04.678
No.

46:09.433 --> 46:11.185
Don't look for me, and just wait.

46:11.977 --> 46:13.854
I'll come find you.

46:16.273 --> 46:17.274
Don't worry.

46:18.692 --> 46:20.652
I know who he is now.

46:23.030 --> 46:23.989
I'll handle it.

46:25.240 --> 46:27.117
What do you think he wants?

46:28.327 --> 46:31.205
Does he want to get back
what was once his? His name?

46:32.039 --> 46:33.248
His place?

46:33.332 --> 46:35.417
No matter what he wants,

46:37.169 --> 46:39.046
what I want is clear,

46:39.838 --> 46:41.673
to leave behind the name Paik Sa-eon…

46:44.259 --> 46:45.928
and start fresh with you.

46:48.555 --> 46:50.599
Let's be happy together.

46:54.937 --> 46:55.938
Go to sleep.

46:57.606 --> 47:00.108
Don't have any bad dreams. Just sleep.

47:02.736 --> 47:04.196
I'll be right here.

48:22.899 --> 48:25.736
JI SANG-WOO

48:26.570 --> 48:28.238
Jeong Jin-seok, I mean…

48:28.322 --> 48:30.407
Jeong Sang-hun is awake.

48:30.490 --> 48:32.534
He'd asked for you the moment he woke up.

48:53.889 --> 48:55.057
You did great.

48:56.308 --> 48:57.309
I'm sorry.

48:58.518 --> 48:59.561
Back then…

49:01.438 --> 49:04.149
I never should've saved him.

49:08.236 --> 49:09.529
Take care of it.

49:09.613 --> 49:11.948
Yes, sir.

49:41.895 --> 49:43.772
I couldn't bring myself to kill…

49:45.816 --> 49:47.567
a child who almost died.

49:48.652 --> 49:50.529
He had lost all his memories.

49:51.571 --> 49:53.281
His mental abilities had weakened.

49:53.365 --> 49:56.785
So I thought it'd be okay
if I quietly looked after him.

49:57.536 --> 49:59.287
But his natural instincts…

50:01.623 --> 50:03.166
remained the same.

50:04.042 --> 50:05.627
Just as you took me in

50:08.088 --> 50:09.715
and raised me as your own,

50:12.968 --> 50:15.262
you couldn't have cast him aside either.

50:21.351 --> 50:22.644
Where are they?

50:23.645 --> 50:25.439
The black bags Paik Jang-ho

50:26.982 --> 50:28.442
asked you to take care of.

50:35.699 --> 50:37.159
I have to find them.

50:38.034 --> 50:39.578
I'll find them…

50:41.621 --> 50:43.039
and expose everything he did.

51:55.070 --> 51:56.238
He's in the hospital?

51:57.614 --> 51:59.991
Yes. It seems he got hurt quite a bit.

52:00.784 --> 52:03.036
But he insists on attending today's event,

52:03.745 --> 52:04.663
so I'm worried.

52:04.746 --> 52:07.457
I wonder what happened this time.

52:07.541 --> 52:08.792
Was he injured badly?

52:08.875 --> 52:10.210
I don't know.

52:10.752 --> 52:12.170
Shouldn't we go see him?

52:12.254 --> 52:13.755
- Where?
- At the hospital.

52:14.589 --> 52:18.051
But would the spokesperson
be happy to see us?

52:18.134 --> 52:19.678
We don't know which hospital.

52:19.761 --> 52:20.679
We do.

52:24.307 --> 52:25.851
- I don't know.
- Again?

52:25.934 --> 52:27.394
Again?

52:27.477 --> 52:31.481
When he says "I don't know,"
we never get what we want to know.

52:32.190 --> 52:35.026
However, don't worry, everyone.

52:35.110 --> 52:38.780
There's a way to find out
which hospital he's in.

52:40.323 --> 52:43.159
But do we have to find out?

52:43.910 --> 52:44.911
I know.

52:44.995 --> 52:46.371
I can hear you.

52:46.454 --> 52:47.330
Here.

52:47.414 --> 52:48.248
Thanks.

52:55.338 --> 52:57.507
The director of Nuri Dream Center told me…

52:59.384 --> 53:00.802
that when we were in college,

53:01.428 --> 53:06.099
you came to volunteer
and were holding a crying baby,

53:06.725 --> 53:09.477
singing a lullaby to calm the baby down.

53:12.230 --> 53:15.817
Good night, my baby

53:16.401 --> 53:20.780
My dear baby

53:20.864 --> 53:24.034
There are beautiful roses

53:25.201 --> 53:29.205
Surrounding you

53:30.248 --> 53:32.250
Good night…

53:32.334 --> 53:36.087
That's right. I think I remember that.

53:36.963 --> 53:38.506
I'm sorry, Sang-woo.

53:38.590 --> 53:40.258
I had no idea.

53:40.342 --> 53:41.593
You're sorry?

53:42.719 --> 53:45.138
I got to hear your voice,

53:46.306 --> 53:47.223
so it's fine.

53:54.356 --> 53:55.815
The spokesperson and I…

53:55.899 --> 53:57.609
Yeah, you don't have to explain.

53:59.027 --> 54:02.781
At first, I was surprised and worried,

54:02.864 --> 54:04.032
but there's one thing…

54:05.492 --> 54:06.451
I'm sure of.

54:11.247 --> 54:15.210
That he's not hiding you
but protecting you.

54:17.796 --> 54:20.215
I face attacks from all sides.

54:21.174 --> 54:24.511
In a way, you could say
I'm the government's official scapegoat.

54:25.261 --> 54:26.846
So I don't want

54:26.930 --> 54:30.100
my wife to be exposed
to indiscriminate attacks like I am.

54:30.183 --> 54:32.936
Yes, she's my weakness.

54:44.114 --> 54:45.657
You're ready to go already?

54:46.908 --> 54:47.993
Yeah.

54:49.327 --> 54:50.370
I'll do it for you.

54:51.913 --> 54:52.998
Do you know how?

54:53.081 --> 54:54.332
How do I do it?

54:55.750 --> 54:56.584
Here.

54:56.668 --> 54:58.253
Grab both ends of the tie.

54:59.379 --> 55:00.380
Cross them over.

55:01.297 --> 55:04.134
Next, loop it here and pull it through.

55:25.905 --> 55:26.781
Is that good?

55:27.323 --> 55:28.241
Great job.

55:31.953 --> 55:34.539
Are you prepared for today's event?

55:35.206 --> 55:36.041
Of course.

55:37.125 --> 55:40.045
But will you really be okay?

55:40.128 --> 55:41.796
I'll be fine.

55:42.589 --> 55:46.051
So you come with the rest of the team.
And be careful.

55:46.551 --> 55:47.385
Okay?

55:58.730 --> 56:00.315
Don't worry about me.

56:00.899 --> 56:02.317
You be careful too.

56:03.860 --> 56:04.694
Okay.

56:15.622 --> 56:17.373
CHIEF KANG YOUNG-WOO

56:22.212 --> 56:23.046
Yes, Mr. Kang.

56:24.172 --> 56:25.423
We're here.

56:26.674 --> 56:27.509
Where?

56:28.051 --> 56:30.011
Didn't you say you'd have it delivered?

56:30.095 --> 56:32.180
No way! We came in person.

56:32.263 --> 56:33.181
Sorry about that.

56:33.890 --> 56:38.103
We've brought your commemorative speech
and your morning coffee.

56:44.275 --> 56:45.110
What?

56:47.112 --> 56:48.905
- The paper.
- Here you go.

56:50.073 --> 56:50.990
And my coffee?

56:52.200 --> 56:53.618
Are you feeling okay?

56:53.701 --> 56:56.538
Yes, I'm fine. I'll see you all later.

56:56.621 --> 56:57.539
Can we come in--

56:57.622 --> 57:00.375
I was just about to go through
the discharge process.

57:00.458 --> 57:02.252
You should all go.

57:02.335 --> 57:04.546
Okay, we'll see you at the event then.

57:08.383 --> 57:10.385
Sir, I'm leading the event today,

57:10.468 --> 57:12.929
so I want to rehearse it with you
before I go.

57:13.012 --> 57:16.057
Once you're done with the process,
we can do it inside…

57:16.141 --> 57:17.767
- Mr. Kang.
- Yes?

57:17.851 --> 57:19.060
Do we still need…

57:20.478 --> 57:21.896
to rehearse it together?

57:22.897 --> 57:25.233
No. Of course not.

57:28.653 --> 57:32.699
You and I are like a well-oiled machine.
We're perfectly in sync, the best team.

57:35.660 --> 57:37.662
- Mr. Park?
- Yes?

57:37.745 --> 57:38.580
Come see me.

57:45.795 --> 57:46.963
2024
ENVIRONMENTAL CLIMATE DAY

57:49.257 --> 57:50.675
Let's sit here.

57:55.221 --> 57:57.056
- Hello.
- How pretty.

58:00.018 --> 58:02.520
2024 ENVIRONMENTAL CLIMATE DAY

58:15.575 --> 58:19.037
Are you ready, Ms. Hong Hee-joo?

58:20.538 --> 58:21.998
Yes, Mr. Paik.

58:23.750 --> 58:25.502
You look a bit nervous.

58:27.337 --> 58:28.838
I'm confident I can do well.

58:30.089 --> 58:32.967
I've been dreaming of this moment
for so long.

58:34.969 --> 58:37.388
I'm looking forward to it too.

58:38.223 --> 58:39.933
The moment I'll stand side by side

58:40.767 --> 58:42.268
with Interpreter Hong Hee-joo.

59:19.556 --> 59:21.391
Greetings,

59:21.474 --> 59:24.602
esteemed citizens and honored guests.

59:25.478 --> 59:27.647
I am Paik Sa-eon,
the Presidential spokesperson.

59:30.191 --> 59:31.276
SPOKESPERSON SPEECH

59:31.359 --> 59:33.903
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo is so impressive.

59:33.987 --> 59:36.990
Of course, I knew it.
She's the best at our center.

59:37.073 --> 59:38.783
So good!

59:38.866 --> 59:41.411
…we often heard that
we were living in an era of extreme

59:41.494 --> 59:42.453
climate change.

59:42.537 --> 59:44.998
I'm so proud. My daughter.

59:46.207 --> 59:47.166
My son-in-law.

59:47.250 --> 59:49.752
…an era of climate "crisis,"
not just "change."

59:49.836 --> 59:51.921
I sincerely hope that this event

59:52.005 --> 59:56.551
will foster constructive discussions
aimed at finding solutions

59:56.634 --> 59:59.429
to climate issues
and presenting new visions.

01:00:00.013 --> 01:00:02.390
I believe that
if we all continue our efforts,

01:00:02.974 --> 01:00:05.351
a better future will come.

01:00:06.102 --> 01:00:07.186
Thank you.

01:00:34.047 --> 01:00:35.590
- Hello?
- Are you busy?

01:00:35.673 --> 01:00:36.841
Yeah, I'm busy.

01:00:36.924 --> 01:00:38.259
You punk.

01:00:38.343 --> 01:00:40.345
That Sinil Childcare Center case.

01:00:40.428 --> 01:00:43.056
I went through everything
and found nothing.

01:00:43.139 --> 01:00:44.015
Does that make sense?

01:00:44.098 --> 01:00:45.642
Is that why you called?

01:00:45.725 --> 01:00:46.934
By the way,

01:00:47.727 --> 01:00:50.730
did you know there were twins
among the missing kids?

01:00:52.315 --> 01:00:53.858
- Twins?
- Yeah.

01:00:53.941 --> 01:00:54.859
So the family

01:00:54.942 --> 01:00:57.278
of the missing person could be out there.

01:00:57.362 --> 01:00:59.697
I mean, the other twin.

01:01:00.281 --> 01:01:01.366
So what?

01:01:01.449 --> 01:01:04.786
One reason this case is difficult
is that the kids are orphans,

01:01:05.453 --> 01:01:07.121
and there are no victim families.

01:01:07.205 --> 01:01:08.665
But if we find the twin…

01:01:09.248 --> 01:01:11.209
We might get a testimony or statement?

01:01:11.292 --> 01:01:12.126
That's right.

01:01:12.710 --> 01:01:14.504
Hey, if anything comes up,

01:01:15.088 --> 01:01:16.506
I get the exclusive interview.

01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:17.590
Got it?

01:01:31.521 --> 01:01:34.148
Yedong-myeon, Sinjeok Mountain.

01:01:34.816 --> 01:01:36.818
You'll find them there.

01:01:37.527 --> 01:01:39.153
I always thought

01:01:40.071 --> 01:01:42.323
that someday the day would come

01:01:42.907 --> 01:01:45.410
when I'd have to atone for my sins.

01:02:02.468 --> 01:02:05.304
The spokesperson asked me
to take you back to the office.

01:02:07.932 --> 01:02:09.308
Great work today.

01:03:30.389 --> 01:03:32.266
HBC JANG HYEOK-JIN

01:03:34.060 --> 01:03:34.894
Hello?

01:03:34.977 --> 01:03:35.812
It's me.

01:03:37.104 --> 01:03:41.484
The police gave me access, so I checked
the missing person's family DNA database.

01:03:41.567 --> 01:03:45.530
I looked for "twins" from Sinil Childcare
Center in Hajeong, Gyeonggi-do in 2000.

01:03:46.155 --> 01:03:47.031
And?

01:03:47.114 --> 01:03:49.951
The younger twin's information
came through.

01:03:52.703 --> 01:03:53.871
I'll send it to you.

01:03:54.497 --> 01:03:55.540
Check it yourself.

01:03:58.835 --> 01:04:00.920
HBC JANG HYEOK-JIN

01:04:01.003 --> 01:04:02.171
PERSONAL RECORDS

01:04:21.274 --> 01:04:22.942
SPOKESPERSON PAIK SA-EON

01:05:07.194 --> 01:05:10.031
NAME: PARK DO-JAE
NAME BEFORE ADOPTION: YUN MIN-SEONG

01:05:14.744 --> 01:05:15.828
HEE-JOO

01:05:18.873 --> 01:05:22.960
The person you're calling is unavailable.
You'll be directed to voicemail.

01:05:23.044 --> 01:05:25.338
Additional fees may apply after the beep.

01:06:21.227 --> 01:06:24.146
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:06:24.230 --> 01:06:25.064
Hee-joo!

01:06:25.648 --> 01:06:26.774
Your name? Your place?

01:06:27.650 --> 01:06:28.776
Do you want them back?

01:06:28.859 --> 01:06:30.403
Will you give me Hong Hee-joo too?

01:06:32.571 --> 01:06:34.407
Where did it all go wrong?

01:06:35.282 --> 01:06:36.409
Do-jae!

01:06:36.492 --> 01:06:38.744
Hurry and come to the memorial service.

01:06:39.412 --> 01:06:40.830
I've got a bad feeling.

01:06:40.913 --> 01:06:42.039
Paik Sa-eon.

01:06:42.123 --> 01:06:44.041
I'm really going to kill her.

01:06:44.917 --> 01:06:46.585
- Your wife.
- Don't come.

01:06:47.753 --> 01:06:48.963
For once,

01:06:49.755 --> 01:06:51.257
I want to protect you.

01:06:52.383 --> 01:06:53.634
I love you.

01:06:58.264 --> 01:07:00.266
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
